---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Notes from the Field" description="Dinesh Pai's curated, high-signal business threads and market observations from his socials.">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-12 py-6 font-serif">
    
    <!-- BACK TO HOME LINK -->
    <div class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider">
      <a href="/" class="text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 hover:text-brand-light dark:hover:text-brand-dark hover:underline inline-flex items-center gap-1">
        &larr; Back to Home
      </a>
    </div>

    <!-- TITLE -->
    <header class="space-y-4">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">
        Notes from the Field
      </h1>
      <p class="font-serif italic text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 text-[17px] sm:text-[20px] border-l-2 border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 pl-4">
        Curated, high-signal business threads, deep-tech observations, and contrarian market insights compiled from my social media channels.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- SEARCH & FILTER INTERFACE -->
    <div class="space-y-4 bg-stone-100 dark:bg-stone-900/40 p-5 rounded-lg border border-stone-200/40 dark:border-stone-800/40">
      <div class="space-y-1.5">
        <label for="notes-search-input" class="font-mono text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-stone-400 dark:text-stone-500 block">
          Search Field Notes
        </label>
        <input 
          type="text" 
          id="notes-search-input" 
          placeholder="Search by topic, keyword, or insight..." 
          class="w-full px-3.5 py-2 rounded border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 bg-white dark:bg-stone-950 font-serif text-sm focus:outline-none focus:border-accent-light dark:focus:border-accent-dark transition-colors duration-200"
        />
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- CURATED NOTES LIST -->
    <div id="notes-list" class="space-y-12">
      
      <!-- NOTE 1: INLAND WATERWAYS -->
      <section class="note-card space-y-4 pb-8 border-b border-dashed border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800" data-search="₹50,000 crore blind spot in indian startups dredging inland waterways national waterways silt conundrum logistics capital markets">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 text-[10px] font-mono font-bold text-stone-400 dark:text-stone-500 uppercase tracking-wide">
          <span>Capital Markets & Logistics</span>
          <span>&bull;</span>
          <span>Feb 22, 2026</span>
        </div>
        
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-black font-serif text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 hover:text-accent-light dark:hover:text-accent-dark transition-colors duration-200">
          The ₹50,000 Crore Blind Spot in Indian Startups: Dredging
        </h2>
        
        <div class="text-stone-800 dark:text-stone-200 leading-relaxed text-[17px] sm:text-[20px] space-y-4 font-serif">
          <p>
            I was going through a newsletter and realized that India is about to spend <strong>₹50,000 crore on inland waterways</strong>. But almost nobody in the startup world is paying attention to dredging. 
          </p>
          <p>
            Here is what I figured:
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-2 pl-5 list-disc">
            <li>
              <strong>111 National Waterways declared:</strong> Over 20,000 km of navigable rivers and canals. But to make them navigable for cargo ships, you need a minimum draft (depth).
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>The Silt Conundrum:</strong> Indian rivers carry some of the highest silt loads in the world due to monsoon runoff. Without continuous, massive dredging operations, these waterways will silt up and choke in a single season.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>The Opportunity:</strong> This is a massive, capital-intensive macro play. It is not about writing software; it's about the physical infrastructure, the supply chain, and the machinery required to move millions of tons of earth daily.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="italic text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 border-l-2 border-dashed border-stone-200/60 dark:border-stone-800/60 pl-4">
            If your business is unsexy, if your sector is muddy, and if your path to scale looks different from what most VC grids recognize—there is massive pricing power waiting for you.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- NOTE 2: INDIGENOUS HARDWARE -->
      <section class="note-card space-y-4 pb-8 border-b border-dashed border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800" data-search="why indigenous hardware is a big deal unit economics cheaper to manufacture scanners rarity moat medical healthcare tech">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 text-[10px] font-mono font-bold text-stone-400 dark:text-stone-500 uppercase tracking-wide">
          <span>Hardware Economics</span>
          <span>&bull;</span>
          <span>Dec 27, 2025</span>
        </div>
        
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-black font-serif text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 hover:text-accent-light dark:hover:text-accent-dark transition-colors duration-200">
          Why Indigenous Hardware is a Big Deal (It's Not Why You Think)
        </h2>
        
        <div class="text-stone-800 dark:text-stone-200 leading-relaxed text-[17px] sm:text-[20px] space-y-4 font-serif">
          <p>
            Btw, just to clarify, when we look at deep-tech investments in local hardware (like medical MRI scanners), the big deal isn't because it's "indigenous" or national pride. 
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>It's a big deal because of unit economics:</strong>
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-2 pl-5 list-disc">
            <li>
              <strong>40% Cheaper to Manufacture:</strong> The team has been able to make the electronics around the magnet extremely well-packaged, reducing manufacturing costs by 40% compared to conventional imported scanners.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>The Rarity Moat (Model 2):</strong> Medical and defense hardware are incredibly hard to build. The regulatory feedback loops are years away and the capital requirements are heavy. But once completed, they command an massive, permanent premium because competition structurally cannot replicate the tech stack.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Took a Village:</strong> It literally took a village to raise this idea. But let's be clear—the founder-entrepreneur is always the one who takes the ultimate risk. Our job as partners is simply to stand beside them and provide patient, non-intrusive support.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- NOTE 3: RAINMATTER MILESTONE -->
      <section class="note-card space-y-4 pb-8 border-b border-dashed border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800" data-search="8 years of rainmatter giving back zerodha's success startups exceptional founders venture ecosystem funding">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 text-[10px] font-mono font-bold text-stone-400 dark:text-stone-500 uppercase tracking-wide">
          <span>Venture & Ecosystem</span>
          <span>&bull;</span>
          <span>Sep 23, 2024</span>
        </div>
        
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-black font-serif text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100 hover:text-accent-light dark:hover:text-accent-dark transition-colors duration-200">
          8 Years of Rainmatter: Giving Back Zerodha's Success
        </h2>
        
        <div class="text-stone-800 dark:text-stone-200 leading-relaxed text-[17px] sm:text-[20px] space-y-4 font-serif">
          <p>
            Eight years since Rainmatter started, today we have:
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-2 pl-5 list-disc">
            <li>
              <strong>100+ startups</strong> backed across multiple verticals.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>130+ exceptional founders</strong> supported across 10+ states.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>660 Crores</strong> in cumulative investment amount.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            As Nithin says, Rainmatter will always be about giving back some of Zerodha's success to the Indian startup ecosystem. We don't have outside LPs, and we don't have exit-driven timelines. We back sustainable, long-term businesses built by operators who love what they build.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>

    <!-- FOOTER DIVIDER -->
    <div class="border-t border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 pt-6 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider">
      <a href="/" class="text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 hover:text-accent-light dark:hover:text-accent-dark hover:underline">
        &larr; Back to Home
      </a>
    </div>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  const searchInput = document.getElementById('notes-search-input') as HTMLInputElement;
  const noteCards = document.querySelectorAll('.note-card');
  
  if (searchInput) {
    searchInput.addEventListener('input', (e) => {
      const query = (e.target as HTMLInputElement).value.toLowerCase().trim();
      
      noteCards.forEach((card) => {
        const searchContent = card.getAttribute('data-search') || '';
        
        // Match query cleanly
        if (searchContent.toLowerCase().includes(query)) {
          card.classList.remove('hidden');
        } else {
          card.classList.add('hidden');
        }
      });
    });
  }
</script>
